WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.540
Darkness

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.880
Stay out of this!

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.460
Chirico!

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.080
Die!

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.670
Chirico!

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.830
Damn! The ammo dump's been ignited! Move it!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:11.790
Yes, sir!

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.790
Chirico!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.750
What happened?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.460
The ammo stores probably blew.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.420
Do you think Chirico...?!

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.130
Oh, God! Chirico's gonna die!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:05.960
Don't move.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.630
Shoot! Why don't you shoot?!

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.000
What would you do in my position?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.880
Kill you without a second's thought!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:19.750
Would you?

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.290
Hey, do you think Chirico's all right?

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.790
Yeah. It was a pretty big explosion, though.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:47.130
Commander, why're you waiting
instead of doing something?!

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.790
Yeah, you big jerk!

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.170
I'm still making my observations.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.880
Besides, he's not going to die.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.080
How would you know?!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.710
That explosion was huge!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.210
And it happened in the middle of battle!

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.170
Even Chirico couldn't handle that!

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:05.290
I said he should've tried to
escape from this planet with us!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.920
Come on, he didn't want to put us in danger!

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.170
Hey! Shut up, all of you!

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:14.000
Treat the civilians nicely, soldier!

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.000
This is AT team.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.920
That explosion in the underground magazine
seems to have destroyed all of the Teltain's forces.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.960
And what about Chirico and Ypsilon?

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.500
Sir! We couldn't find either of their ATs.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.540
We checked one of the deep tunnels,
but it's completely sealed off.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.630
They're probably down there. Dig them out!

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.710
It'll take some time, sir.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:38.040
Hurry up! Chirico's gonna die!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:38.750
Huh?

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.330
Hurry! Just save him! Come on!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.290
I said get to work!

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.540
Chirico!

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:49.250
Hey, we're civilians, remember?! Civilians!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.670
He's alive. I know he is.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.080
Just wait quietly and you'll be all right.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.960
Chirico...

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.540
Well? Are you in over there?

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.040
No! No good!

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:18.420
If you're thinking of killing me,
you can do it any time.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:23.380
You don't want to fight me
because I have no weapons?

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.380
If I were in your shoes, I'd show you no mercy!

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.040
We're completely sealed in here.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:37.880
My ATs legs are wrecked,
and you have no weapons.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:39.540
Are you sure you still want to fight?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.750
We have to end this!

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.000
And you can do it, right now!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:52.130
There, the situation's reversed.
What do you do now?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.580
What are you playing at?!

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.960
This is the Teltain! Ypsilon, come in!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.750
What is your condition, Ypsilon?!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.630
Why don't you shoot me?
It's what you want, isn't it?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.170
This can't be...

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.540
Or won't your pride as a PS let you?

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.960
I was thinking of getting out of here.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.790
If you want to shoot me, then shoot.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:27.040
Otherwise, two people can dig faster than one.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.670
Wouldn't you agree?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.960
Is Chirico... Are they both all right?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.380
You're worried about him, aren't you?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.250
They seem to have fallen into
an underground tunnel.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.790
They're probably still fighting down there.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:58.420
We should know its conclusion soon.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.460
When we find out which one is still alive.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.170
You set up this battle between
Chirico and Ypsilon, didn't you?!

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:11.460
Ypsilon is a PS,
so why is Chirico his equal in battle?

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.330
That is what interests me.

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:14.830
That isn't the only thing!

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.040
Oh?

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.130
You know something else about Chirico.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.040
Something?

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.420
Yes... Something!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.330
Are you just going to sit there?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.250
Are you going to help me or kill me?

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.750
Hurry up and decide!

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.290
There's one thing I want to ask you.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:04.580
What?

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.880
Why have you been fighting me?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.630
Because you've been after me.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.920
And that's the only reason?!

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.750
No, not just that. Because...

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:18.750
To protect her?

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.380
To protect your friends?

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:23.460
I don't really know for sure.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.630
Maybe it's because you and I are the same.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:26.630
No, we're not!

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.750
You and I are nothing alike!

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.580
The only person like me is Proto One!

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.130
She and I are chosen warriors.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:39.960
Your existence and mine
share nothing in common!

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.540
You must have a past of your own.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.130
Why were you chosen to be a PS?

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.170
I have no past!

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.290
Just like Proto One doesn't have one!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.790
Fyana's-

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:56.580
Why do you call her Fyana?!

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:58.710
Why?

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:02.630
Good question. Why DO I call her Fyana?

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.750
Why?! Answer me!

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.670
Why won't you tell me?!

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.250
Answer me, Chirico!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.040
Tell me why!

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:17.330
I don't know why. Maybe there is no reason.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:24.830
So, are you going to help me or not?

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.170
I'm not doing this because of what you said.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.630
I'm doing this out of pride.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.790
I'm sure.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.500
This is the search team!

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.790
We've picked up life readings
from underground tunnel #3.

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.710
They're strong and definitely human!

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:28.670
Rochina here! That's them! Roll the earth-movers!

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:30.170
Yes, sir! Rolling!

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.670
Looks like they're okay.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:36.210
He's alive! He's alive!

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:38.330
I knew he was alive!

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:39.920
Chirico's alive!

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:43.580
Yeah, he's a lucky SOB. I don't think he can die!

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.500
He's immortal, all right.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.920
He isn't a normal man, that's for sure!

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.580
A normal man?

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.420
No, not normal by any means.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.330
This is taking too long!

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:10.130
Ypsilon's AT team was apparently
caught in an explosion.

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.080
It looks like they were all destroyed.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.000
The real question is Ypsilon.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.670
The scout ship's coming into range.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:17.130
It should have more intelligence for us.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:21.000
I hope it'll say he's avoided
getting captured by the Balarant!

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:25.250
Sir, we still don't know if they've
learned our position yet.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.170
In any event, we can't let them have Ypsilon.

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:32.880
The experiment's run into
unexpected trouble, eh, Arron?

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:37.380
Quite. This annoying problem will render our
previously gathered data meaningless.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.710
We still don't know that.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:43.250
If we can recover Ypsilon, we may be able
to get the data on their battle.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:46.790
All sorts of problems have
accompanied this experiment.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.580
Video from the scout ship, sir.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:54.290
This is scout ship 3.
We've intercepted enemy transmissions.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.250
Our AT team has been destroyed.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:59.210
Ypsilon and Chirico are alive,
but are trapped underground.

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.960
The Balarant are attempting to dig them out.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.130
Ypsilon's alive...?

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:06.960
This area's too hot to stay in! Pulling out!

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:09.000
Understood! Return to ship at once!

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.330
Roger!

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.080
We've done it.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:18.750
Yes. We'll see exactly how being sealed in has
changed his psychology and adaptabilty index.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:22.540
Yes, assuming we're able to recover him.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.460
True, which may well be impossible.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:29.000
We may not know his condition,
but they mustn't get Ypsilon!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:31.130
Send out an AT rescue team!

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:31.790
Sir!

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:34.420
We have to succeed!

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:19.710
Looks like your oxygen's running out.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.880
It may be wiser for us to wait and be rescued.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.750
You're afraid of dying?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.500
To be honest, yes, I want to live.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.580
For Proto One's sake?

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.330
I hate you. Both of you!

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:50.750
Proto One and I are the only two of our kind.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.000
And so...

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:58.290
I thought, since we were both born as PSs,
our future together was decided.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.130
A future of glorious combat.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:03.130
There is no glory in combat.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:07.830
There is for me,
because I am a Perfect Soldier!

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.750
Only because you think there is.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:15.540
No! I know there is! I'm a PS! I'm special!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.420
You were originally an ordinary man.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:19.880
You're modified, that's all.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.830
You don't understand!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.830
I represent an existence
that surpasses a mere human's!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:26.790
I pity you.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.210
You what?!

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.250
You haven't surpassed anything.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.500
Your thoughts are locked onto only one subject.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.500
You're just a well-honed human weapon!

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:41.420
You dare to criticize me, one of the chosen?!

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:44.460
You, an ordinary human, dares...?!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.790
That pride you cling to is meaningless.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:48.920
What?!

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:52.250
If you keep getting excited,
you'll use up your oxygen.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:53.880
You'd better just calm down.

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.170
I am a PS.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:02.790
To face an enemy and destroy him
is my highest purpose. A glorious one!

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:28.330
There's only one point where you and I are similar.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:36.290
For some reason, you can fight as well as I can.

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.710
I'll bet you don't even know why.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.330
Looks like they've noticed us.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.420
Yeah.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:00.170
We're in! Prepare to rescue them!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:03.040
Chirico! Chirico Cuvie! Can you hear me?

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.500
If you can, make a sound to lead us to you!

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.540
Chirico! Chirico Cuvie!

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:14.580
Mark me, Chirico. I will come back to kill you.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:18.040
I know. I wasn't thinking of running away from you.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.830
What about the other one?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:41.250
Give me a spare oxygen cannister.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:42.790
We've got one ready.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.540
The other guy's alive, isn't he?

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.500
Yeah, he is. But he got away.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:48.580
What?!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.420
Go inside and check it out!

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:51.080
Sir!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.080
We're here for you, sir!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.040
There's a spare oxygen cannister in the AT.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.710
We brought it here on remote control.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.380
Right. Good work.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.540
Got 'em! Over there!

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:22.830
Try to take him alive! Don't kill him!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.130
Ypsilon...

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:49.880
It looks like Ypsilon got away.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.710
He'll be back.

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:57.380
I see. You've agreed to a rematch.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.540
When is it?

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.170
Are my friends all right?

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:03.580
They will be as long as you keep your promise.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.080
I'll tell you when the time comes.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:14.880
All right. I'll release your friends.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:22.080
Chirico... You're all right!

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:25.080
Chirico, you're alive!

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:27.420
Our battle isn't over yet.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.750
Ypsilon will be back.

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:33.750
Stop it. There'll never be an end to this.

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:38.130
Yes, there will be. When one of us is dead.

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.380
Chirico...

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:44.380
I'm going to fight him. I have to.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.330
No...

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:49.790
And I think this next battle will be our last.

00:22:09.670 --> 00:22:13.250
Chirico... He's staying here just for our sake.

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:17.790
Yeah, and he's gonna fight that monster again.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:20.290
He'll get through it. I know he will.

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:30.080
It seemed Rochina had kept his promise.

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:34.130
My final battle with Ypsilon...

00:22:34.670 --> 00:22:36.580
The time was fast approaching.

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:40.420
Will I survive it, or will he?

00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:46.380
And if I do survive, what then?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:00.830
The bullet he fires strikes his image in a mirror.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:04.830
His image vanishes as the fragments scatter.

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:11.880
Far across the sea of space he is led on
by a mirror with another image of him.

00:23:11.880 --> 00:23:13.080
Led to the planet Quent.

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:16.420
Next time, "Perfect Soldier"

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.790
What is the secret which lies
hidden inside his body?

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Perfect Soldier

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
